PTX warpspeed-reader-side-proxy-fence
"Proxy fence on the consumer side: writer threads store to smem and arrive on an mbarrier; the leader waits on it, then fence.proxy.async.shared::cta, then stores the buffer to global with a bulk copy (CCCL cub/detail/warpspeed/resource/smem_resource_raw.cuh:143-183, cub/detail/warpspeed/squad/load_store.cuh:262-268, 364-365). CUTLASS puts the fence on the writer side; here it follows the acquire. The copy must store the new value 1. Expected: forbidden."
{
s=0 @cta 0;
g=9;
m=mbarrier(1) @cta 0;
P1:r0=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0      | P1@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0                         ;
 st.weak.shared::cta s, 1      | mbarrier.try_wait.parity.acquire.cta r0, m, 0    ;
 mbarrier.arrive.release.cta m | fence.proxy.async.shared::cta                    ;
                               | cp.async.bulk.global.shared::cta.bulk_group g, s ;
                               | cp.async.bulk.commit_group                       ;
                               | cp.async.bulk.wait_group.read 0                  ;
exists
(P1:r0 == 1 /\ g == 0)
